A
Appendix: How it works
There's nothing exotic in the stack. Most of the effort went into making the AI predictable. The model can only answer
through a fixed schema, and the server checks every response before anyone sees it.
EVERY AI REQUEST FOLLOWS THE SAME PATH
Browser
›
Rate limit
›
Validate input
›
Forced tool call
›
Check shape
›
Retry once
›
Clean output
Most of the reliability comes from the two highlighted steps. If both attempts fail, the user sees a plain error and can try again.
STACK
LAYERCHOICEWHY
AppNext.js 16, React 19, TypeScriptPages load fast and search engines can read them. AI responses
are typed and checked at runtime.
AIClaude API with forced tool callsThe model returns structured data, never free text the interface
has to guess at. The model choice lives in one place.
GuardrailsServer-side validation and one retryBad output gets rejected instead of shown.
StorageBrowser only, no sign-upNothing to sign up for, and decisions stay on the user's device.
SafetyUpstash Redis rate limiting20 requests per hour per route keeps a free public tool affordable
to run.
HardeningSecurity headersHSTS, nosniff, a referrer policy, same-origin framing, and a
permissions policy.
ReachEnglish and Spanish on VercelEach language has its own routes, and the model answers in the
visitor's language with its own writing rules.
THREE API ROUTES, EACH LOCKED TO A SCHEMA
/api/analyze
Reads the situation back with source
quotes and an "I noticed" line, then
generates options with cost, risk, and
reversibility.
/api/decide
Turns a committed decision into a
summary and a draft for each
audience.
/api/rewrite
Rewrites one draft, shorter or more
direct, without redoing the whole
decision.
